---
/**
 * /returns — Returns & Refunds. The official policy for physical wall calendars (terms in
 * src/data/support.ts → POLICY, approved 2026-10-16), plus the separate, already-published
 * 30-day guarantee on downloads. Other physical goods (the mug) and personalized products have
 * no published terms yet: add their own section before they go on sale, never reuse the
 * calendar's. The return address is never published or stored in code: the owner sends it by hand (private email
 * or Etsy Messages) once a return is approved (docs/operations/CUSTOMER_SUPPORT.md).
 * Operating steps behind each promise: docs/operations/CUSTOMER_SUPPORT.md. /refunds redirects here.
 */
import PublicLayout from '../layouts/PublicLayout.astro';
import { ETSY, POLICY, RESPONSE_TIME, SUPPORT_EMAIL, policyDate } from '../data/support';
import { routes } from '../routes';

const days = POLICY.returnWindowDays;
const h2 = 'serif-title mt-12 text-[1.5rem] sm:text-[1.75rem]';
const p = 'mt-3 text-[1rem] leading-relaxed text-warm-ink';
const a = 'underline decoration-warm-rule decoration-1 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-warm-ink';
const list = 'mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-[1rem] leading-relaxed text-warm-ink';
const sections = [
  { id: 'window', label: `The ${days}-day window` },
  { id: 'how', label: 'How to request a return' },
  { id: 'damaged', label: 'Damaged or incorrect orders' },
  { id: 'refunds', label: 'Refunds' },
  { id: 'cancel', label: 'Cancellations' },
  { id: 'shipping', label: 'Shipping problems' },
  { id: 'etsy', label: 'Bought on Etsy' },
  { id: 'downloads', label: 'Downloads' },
];
---

<PublicLayout
  title="Returns & Refunds"
  description={`Returns within ${days} days of delivery on unused wall calendars, free replacements or refunds for damaged or incorrect orders, and how refunds work for Etsy and website orders.`}
  width="full"
>
  <section aria-labelledby="returns-h" class="public-panel public-intro">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-12 sm:px-8 sm:py-16">
      <p class="label text-warm-soft">Policies</p>
      <h1 id="returns-h" class="serif-hero mt-3">Returns &amp; Refunds</h1>
      <p class="lede mt-5 text-warm-ink">We want you to feel good about your purchase. If something isn’t right, here’s how we’ll help.</p>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row sm:items-center">
        <a href={routes.supportContact} class="btn-primary min-h-14 px-7 text-center">Request Help With an Order</a>
        <a href={ETSY.purchases} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link text-warm-ink sm:ml-3"
          >Bought on Etsy? Message us there<span class="sr-only"> (opens Etsy)</span></a
        >
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6 text-[0.9rem] text-warm-soft">Effective <time datetime={POLICY.effective}>{policyDate()}</time>. Applies to our printed family wall calendars.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pt-10 pb-16 sm:px-8 sm:pb-24">
    <nav aria-labelledby="toc-h" class="border-y border-warm-rule py-5">
      <h2 id="toc-h" class="label text-warm-soft">On this page</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-x-6 gap-y-2 sm:grid-cols-2">
        {sections.map((s) => <li><a href={`#${s.id}`} class={`${a} text-[0.98rem] text-warm-ink`}>{s.label}</a></li>)}
      </ul>
    </nav>

    <h2 id="window" class={h2}>Our {days}-day return window</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      You can return a calendar within {days} calendar days of confirmed delivery. Your calendar is dated, week by week, so we keep the window
      short: a returned calendar is only useful to another family while its weeks are still ahead.
    </p>
    <p class={p}>To be eligible for a change-of-mind return:</p>
    <ul class={list}>
      <li>Contact us within {days} days of delivery to request it.</li>
      <li>The calendar is unused and in its original, resalable condition: nothing written in, no missing or torn pages.</li>
      <li>You have proof of purchase, such as your order number or receipt.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class={p}>There are no restocking fees.</p>
    <p class={p}>
      We don’t offer direct exchanges for change-of-mind returns. If you’d like a different calendar, return the unused one within {days} days and
      order the one you want. If we sent the wrong calendar or it arrived damaged, we’ll replace it for free (below).
    </p>

    <h2 id="how" class={h2}>How to request a return</h2>
    <ol class="mt-3 list-decimal space-y-2 pl-6 text-[1rem] leading-relaxed text-warm-ink">
      <li>
        Message us within {days} days of delivery with your order number. Etsy orders: use Etsy Messages. Website orders: use our{' '}
        <a href={routes.supportContact} class={a}>support form</a> or email <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`} class={a}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        Once your return is approved, we’ll send you the return address and shipping instructions by email (or Etsy Messages for Etsy orders).
        Please don’t send anything before then.
      </li>
      <li>Ship the calendar back. For change-of-mind returns, return shipping is yours to pay; a trackable service protects you.</li>
      <li>We’ll let you know when it arrives and start your refund.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2 id="damaged" class={h2}>Damaged, defective or incorrect orders</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      If your calendar arrives damaged, has a printing or binding defect, or isn’t what you ordered, we’ll send a free replacement or a refund at no
      additional cost to you. The {days}-day return window doesn’t apply here: let us know whenever you notice the problem (sooner is easier to sort
      out with the carrier). Send us your order number and, if you can, a photo: it helps us sort it out quickly. You
      usually won’t need to send the calendar back; if we do need it, we’ll cover the cost and tell you how.
    </p>

    <h2 id="refunds" class={h2}>Refunds</h2>
    <ul class={list}>
      <li>We start your refund within {POLICY.refundStartBusinessDays} business days of receiving and checking the returned calendar.</li>
      <li>
        Refunds go back through the platform you bought on, to your original payment method, as far as that platform allows: Etsy orders through
        Etsy, website orders through our secure checkout. Your bank may take a few more days to show it.
      </li>
      <li>For change-of-mind returns, the original shipping cost isn’t refundable.</li>
      <li>For damaged, defective or incorrect orders, refunds include shipping.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="cancel" class={h2}>Cancellations</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      You can cancel before your order ships. Message us as soon as you can and we’ll check where it is in packing. If it has already shipped, we
      can’t stop it, but it can come back as a return.
    </p>

    <h2 id="shipping" class={h2}>Shipping problems and lost packages</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      If your tracking stops moving or a package goes missing, message us. We’ll look into each one individually with the carrier and, for Etsy
      orders, with Etsy, and let you know what happens next.
    </p>

    <h2 id="late" class="serif-title mt-12 text-[1.25rem]">Outside the {days} days?</h2>
    <p class={p}>Contact us anyway. We’ll look at your situation individually.</p>

    <section aria-labelledby="etsy" class="mt-12 bg-sage-wash p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h2 id="etsy" class="serif-title text-[1.5rem] sm:text-[1.75rem]">Bought on Etsy?</h2>
      <p class={p}>
        Message us through Etsy for anything about that order. Etsy Messages keeps your order details in one place, so we can help you fastest.
        Approved refunds for Etsy orders are issued through Etsy to your original payment method, and Etsy’s own buyer policies also apply.
      </p>
      <ol class="mt-3 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-6 text-[1rem] leading-relaxed text-warm-ink">
        <li>Open <strong>Purchases</strong> in your Etsy account.</li>
        <li>Find your calendar order and message us from there.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="mt-5 flex flex-col gap-2 sm:flex-row sm:gap-6">
        <a href={ETSY.purchases} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link text-warm-ink"
          >Open your Etsy purchases<span class="sr-only"> (opens Etsy)</span></a
        >
        <a href={ETSY.shop} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link text-warm-ink"
          >Visit our Etsy shop<span class="sr-only"> (opens Etsy)</span></a
        >
      </p>
    </section>

    <h2 id="downloads" class={h2}>Downloads</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      The calendar terms above are for printed calendars only. Every download (the Weekly Reset System, Take Back Control, the Essential Routines
      Bundle and the Real Life Reset Kit) comes with a 30-day money-back guarantee. Use it for 30 days from your purchase. If it isn’t helping, email
      us and we’ll refund every penny. No questions asked, nothing to send back. Once you’re refunded, your download link stops working.
    </p>

    <h2 class="serif-title mt-12 text-[1.25rem]">The cleaning companion</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      The <a href={routes.companion} class={a}>cleaning companion website</a> comes with your calendar at no extra cost and isn’t sold
      separately, so there’s nothing to return or cancel.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-14 border-t border-warm-rule pt-8">
      <p class="font-serif text-[1.25rem] leading-snug text-warm-ink">Still have a question?</p>
      <p class={p}>
        {RESPONSE_TIME} <a href={routes.support} class={a}>Visit Help &amp; Support</a> or email{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`} class={a}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</PublicLayout>
